50\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nStep 9-1. Short Thesis (5-7 bullets):\n1. At 27.8x FY26 EPS and 18.8x EV/EBITDA, the market pays for flawless 5-year execution; any deceleration (already visible: H2'26 implied +14.5% vs Q2 +22.2%) triggers multiple compression.\n2. Grizzly Research (Nov 2024) documented: transfer of China storefront entity to chairman-controlled Joyoung for nominal consideration; $665M pre-IPO dividends/loans; ~$3B related-party purchases 2021-23; 28-year-old son of chairman on board. The company's detailed rebuttal is not in our data [Unconfirmed] \u2014 the opacity itself is a red flag.\n3. No recurring revenue: hardware units with replacement cycles of 3-7 years; consumables attachment is immaterial. The \"compounder\" label is based on a hardware treadmill.\n4. Core category (cleaning, +4.1% Q2'26) is decelerating toward market growth; 41 subcategories means the marginal subcategory gets smaller.\n5. Tariffs annualizing at 12.5% from China/Vietnam/Thailand; the $247.1M Q3 refund is one-time and non-recurring.\n6. Net margin 8.6-11% [Aggregator vs Arithmetic] vs competitors' average profitability: limited pricing power in a value-priced portfolio.\n7. 12.9% short interest and 68.6% institutional ownership \u2014 if fundamentals crack, the exit door is narrow.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic Combat Scores (1-10):\n- Long logic: 6/10 (execution, international runway, balance sheet).\n- Short logic: 5/10 (valuation + governance + category decel; but the governance claim is from a short-seller with a position, 22 months old, unproven in court/SEC).\nGap = 1 < 2 \u2192 CONVICTION DOWNGRADE (Medium, per Section 5). This closes the gap: I do not short this name despite the negative expected return (gap is too small; risk of a continued squeeze).\n\nStep 9-3. Adversarial data: Grizzly Research (Nov 2024), \"We Believe SharkNinja is a China Hustle\u2026\" [Actual source, unverified claims]. The stock survived the report initially but has sin