ice $55-75, a -60 to -70% drawdown from T0. Portfolio CVaR contribution if held at 5% weight: additional ~3% portfolio loss in that tail.\n- Cross-position check: if the portfolio already holds consumer-discretionary/growth names, SN adds concentrated factor risk. Recommendation: if held, cap 2%; if not held, no initiation.\n\nSECTION 8. MONITORING RULES\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStep 7-1. Thesis integrity thresholds (re-evaluate immediately if breached):\n1. Gross margin < 48% for 2 consecutive quarters (tariffs/pricing failure)\n2. Cleaning segment growth negative growth for 2 consecutive quarters (core brand erosion)\n3. Beauty + Home Environment growth\n\nBelow +10% for 2 quarters (fashion cycle peak)\n4. FCF conversion (cumulative 4-qtr OCF/4-qtr NI) < 0.80 (working-capital trap)\n5. Revenue growth < 12% for 2 consecutive quarters (fade arriving early)\n6. Inventory growth > 1.5x revenue growth for 2 consecutive quarters (channel stuffing risk)\n7. Related-party purchase disclosures expand beyond current levels, or auditor/CFO change (governance escalation)\n8. FY27 revenue guidance < +8% (my fade case arriving)\n\nStep 7-4. PRE-MORTEM: \"It's 2031; SN is at $45. Why?\"\n1. Viral-franchise exhaustion: CREAMi/FlexStyle/ChillPill cycle ended; no new subcategory hit; growth fell to 2-3%; multiple de-rated to 15x. Early warning: beauty/cooking growth <10% for 2 qtrs; new-category contribution <5% of revenue.\n2. Tariff + competition squeeze: GM fell to 44%; share loss to Chinese entrants (Joyoung-linked?); international expansion reversed. Early warning: GM <48%; international growth <15%.\n3. Governance event crystallizes: SEC inquiry into related-party transfers; restatement; founder control discount of 40%+; short interest >20%. Early warning: disclosure of new related-party transactions; auditor resignation; CFO exit; Grizzly follow-up report with new evidence.\n\nStep 7-5. DECISION JOURNAL ENTRY (see Section 11).\n\nSECTION 9. RED TEAM & ADVERSARIAL ANALYSIS\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStep 9-1. Short Thesis (5-7 bullets, using the SAME data):\n1. Valuation: 36.8x trailing GAAP EPS, 27.8x forward non-GAAP, 3.4x forward EV/Sales, 18.7x EV/EBITDA for a company with ZERO recurring revenue, 67% 5-yr cumulative FCF conversion, and a CEO who publicly doubts growth durability. Negative expected value: -23% to my expected price.\n2. Governance (Grizzly Research, 2024-11-21 [Actual - short report]): SharkNinja (China) Technology - holder of the only official-looking SharkNinja storefronts on JD.com and Tmall - was transferred to a chairman-controlled entity for nominal consideration; $665M pre-IPO special dividends/related-party loans funded in part by >$300M added debt; $3B+ related-party purchases 2021-2023; chairman's son (28) on board; chairman also controls Joyoung (supplier). Market dismissed it at $94; at $180 it is a margin-of-safety destroyer.\n3. Fashion risk: 65% growth in Beauty/Home and 37% in Cooking cannot be extrapolated; cleaning (+4.1%) shows what \"mature\" looks like. The company is a sum of viral product cycles - historically mean-reverting.\n4. Tariff structural drag: FY26 guide embedded 19-20% tariffs; Q2 call cited a new 12.5% rate on China/Vietnam/Thailand goods; the $247M Q3 refund is a ONE-TIME margin flatter.\n5. Working capital: 5-yr cumulative FCF $1.261B vs NI $1.870B (67%); inventory $1.14B +8.6%; receivables $1.667B and growing ~15%. Reported FCF overstates distributable cash.\n6. One-sided consensus: 13/13 buys, zero sells/holds, low target 8% ABOVE price, low target above 52-week high. When consensus is this uniform, the marginal buyer is gone; the marginal seller is all that remains.\n7. Crowding/positioning: 68.6% institutional, 12.9% short - if growth decelerates, passive fund outflows and short pressure compound downside.\n\nStep 9-2. Logic Combat (Long vs Short):\n- Long evidence 