\n\u25cf Cost advantage: 2 \u2014 scale in sourcing and global logistics, but heavily exposed to Chinese/SEA manufacturing (tariffs).\n\u25cf Economies of scale: 2 \u2014 R&D and marketing leveraged over $7.4B sales, but the category (floor care) also has scale incumbents.\n\u25cf Regulatory barriers: 1 \u2014 modest: safety standards, tariffs/EU compliance.\n\u25cf Data moat: 1 \u2014 POS data and AI (60% capture accuracy) help cycle speed; not proprietary in a defensible way.\nTOTAL: 10/21 \u2014 NARROW MOAT. Moat direction: STABLE. Widening evidence: +22% growth in a flat category, share gains, 41st subcategory. Narrowing evidence: cleaning segment decelerated to +4.1% in Q2'26, comps are entering (Ulta distribution for ChillPill shows they must seek new channels), competitors with comparable Chinese supply chains.\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch Classification: FAST GROWER. Core checkpoint: sustained 15%+ growth requires new category after new category (CREAMi \u2192 Luxe Caf\u00e9 \u2192 Crispi \u2192 FlexStyle \u2192 ChillPill). This is SN's model and it is working today; the question is durability. For a fast-grower, valuation must not outrun the growth; at 27.8x forward P/E and PEG 2.87 (trailing [Actual \u2014 Aggregator]), the market is paying above the Lynch 1.0-1.5 PEG comfort boundary.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard [all Actual \u2014 filed unless noted]:\n\n\u25cf Revenue growth: FY21-25 4-yr CAGR = +14.5% [Arithmetic]; FY25 +15.7% [Arithmetic]; FY26E +16-17% (guidance) [Actual \u2014 company].\n\u25cf Operating margin: FY25 14.4% [Arithmetic]; TTM 14.4% [Arithmetic]; FY26E ~15.5% [Estimate].\n\u25cf EPS: FY25 diluted EPS $4.93 [Arithmetic]; FY26E $6.45-6.55 [Actual \u2014 guidance].\n\u25cf ROE: 27.5% [Aggregator]. ROIC: ~19% [Estimate \u2014 NOPAT $533M at 24% tax [Assumption], invested capital = equity $2.676B + LT debt $0.697B + current debt $0.039B + operating leases $0.165B \u2212 cash $0.777B = $2.800B].\n\u25cf FCF margin: FY25 $488M/6,399 = 7.6%