TED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n\u25cf R&D capitalization: SN does not separate R&D; engineering is inside SG&A ($390M FY25 = 6.1% of sales) [Actual \u2014 filed]. Cannot capitalize separately [Unconfirmed]. My model treats all SG&A as operating expense; if one capitalized 50% of SG&A as 4-yr amortized, adjusted EBIT would rise ~$120-150M (\u2248+2% margin) and invested capital up ~$600M. Adjusted ROIC impact: +0.5-1.0pp. Immaterial to the conclusion at the current price.\n\u25cf SBC treatment: SBC FY25 $44M [Actual \u2014 filed]. I deduct SBC as an expense in FCF: Adjusted FY25 FCF = $488M \u2212 $44M = $444M [Arithmetic]. TTM adjusted FCF \u2248 $761M [Estimate]. SBC is not a rounding error; at 0.7% of revenue, it is also not a dealbreaker.\n\u25cf Operating lease capitalization: FY25 operating leases $165M [Actual \u2014 filed]. Capitalized at 8x = $1.32B; adjusted net debt becomes $1.44B; net debt/adjusted EBITDA ~1.1x. Still healthy. A 9.7% WACC already includes lease-like debt at ~4.2% after tax, consistent.\n\u25cf Adjusted ROIC: my ~19% ROIC is 2.5pp above WACC \u2014 a genuine value creator, but not a fortress. If R&D were capitalized and SBC expensed, adjusted ROIC is ~20%. The gap vs GAAP is <5pp.\n\u25cf Owner earnings (FY25): NI $701M + D&A $140M \u2212 maintenance capex (est. 50% of $146M = $73M [Assumption]) \u2212 \u0394WC $723M [Arithmetic] = $45M. Owner earnings were depressed by the 2025 working-capital build (inventory +$0.10B, receivables +$0.40B). TTM shows the release (OCF $974M vs NI $695M [Arithmetic]): owner earnings TTM \u2248 $455M after SBC [Estimate]. Conclusion: cash conversion is lumpy; do not use a single-year FCF for the DCF without smoothing (Section 3).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3 \u2014 VALUATION (ENGINE 1 \u2014 DCF + MULTIPLES)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nEngine selection rationale:\n(1) Archetype B (Quality Compounder): high ROIC (~19% vs 9.7% WACC), positive FCF, consistent margins, low leverage.\n(2) NOT Engine 2 (Cyclical) because SN's consumer category growth has been structurally positive; the cycle is not the dominant driver.\n(3) NOT Engine 4 (Option) because the core monetization is hardware sales; AI/social commerce are enablers, not standalone option value.\n(4) NOT Engine 5 (Binary) \u2014 no single approval event.\nNo archetype transition applies: core revenue is 100% of revenue; no platform/installed-base monetization disclosed [Unconfirmed]. If a recurring-revenue stream evolves (consumables, subscription), the archetype would migrate to D (Hybrid); trigger not yet met.\n\nStep 3-1. Discount Rate Derivation:\n\n\u25cf Risk-free rate = 4.7% [Actual \u2014 10Y UST, TradingEconomics 2026-08-21].\n\u25cf Equity risk premium = 4.75% [Assumption \u2014 long-run historical, anchored to current elevated Rf].\n\u25cf Beta: 1.1 [Assumption \u2014 vendor beta 1.168 [Aggregator] blended with fundamental beta ~1.0 for a consumer-discretionary hardware business with 41% insider ownership and low debt; I underweight the vendor beta because its window/benchmark is unstated].\n\u25cf Cost of equity = 4.7% + 1.1 \u00d7 4.75% = 9.93%.\n\u25cf Pre-tax cost of debt = 5.5% [Assumption \u2014 BB+/BBB- synthetic for SN's capital structure].\n\u25cf Effective tax rate = 24% [Assumption \u2014 pack withheld tax; identity NI+tax=PTI holds, but consolidated rate not derivable from pack. 24% reflects US federal + state + international mix. I label this mine.]\n\u25cf After-tax Kd = 5.5% \u00d7 (1 \u2212 0.24) = 4.18%.\n\u25cf Weights: E = $25.472B, D = debt+leases $0.901B \u2192 E = 96.6%, D = 3.4%.\n\u25cf WACC = 0.966 \u00d7 9.93% + 0.034 \u00d7 4.18% = 9.73%. Rounded: 9.7%.\n\nStep 3-2. Explicit Forecast (per-year) \u2014 FY2026E through FY2030E:\n\nBasis: FY2026 = company guidance [Actual]: revenue $7.45B (midpoint of $7.4-7.5B); adj EBITDA $1.365B (midpoint); capex $200M (midpoint of $190-210M). Adj EPS $6.50 (midpoint $6.45-6.55, incl. $0.15 one-time tariff refund \u2014 I exclude that $0.15 from going-forward EPS).\n\nRevenue path beyond FY2026 is my own [Assumption], informed by: (a) FY26 guidance implies H2'26 +14.5% (Arithmetic: H2'26E $4.272B vs H2'25 $3.731B) \u2014 already decelerating from Q2's +22.2%; (b) sell-side full-year FY27 consensus \u2248 +11-12% [Estimate \u2014 Yahoo/MarketWatch next-year estimates]; (c) 4-yr company CAGR 14.5% [Arithmetic]; (d) base rate of category growth ~4-6% [Assumption].\n\n| $B | FY26E | FY27E | FY28E | FY29E | FY30E |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Revenue growth | +16.5% | +11.0% | +8.0% | +6.0% | +6.0% |\n| Revenue | 7.45 | 8.27 | 8.93 | 9.47 | 10.04 |\n| EBIT margin | 15.5% | 15.8% | 16.0% | 16.2% | 16.5% |\n| EBIT | 1.155 | 1.307 | 1.429 | 1.534 | 1.657 |\n| Taxes @24% | 0.277 | 0.314 | 0.343 | 0.368 | 0.398 |\n| NOPAT | 0.878 | 0.993 | 1.086 | 1.166 | 1.259 |\n| + D&A | 0.175 | 0.190 | 0.205 | 0.220 | 0.235 |\n| \u2212 Capex | 0.200 | 0.220 | 0.240 | 0.260 | 0.280 |\n| \u2212 \u0394WC | 0.100 | 0.150 | 0.150 | 0.120 | 0.120 |\n| FCF | 0.753 | 0.813 | 0.901 | 1.006 | 1.094 |\n\nMargin path justification: FY26 GAAP EBIT margin \u2248 15.5% = adjusted EBITDA 18.3% [Actual \u2014 guidance] minus D&A ~2.4% minus SBC ~0.4% [Estimate]. Margin expansion thereafter: slower, +0.2-0.3pp/yr, because (a) tariff annualization at 12.5% (Q2'26 disclosure) [Actual], (b) five-year median operating margin 11.7% [Arithmetic] shows historic volatility, (c) category competition limits price. Terminal EBIT margin 16.5% is ABOVE SN's own 5-year median \u2014 arguably optimistic. Working capital: I smooth the 2025 build; assume +$0.10-0.15B/yr (inventory for new launches, receivables from international/social channels) [Assumption].\n\nTERMINAL: g = 3.5% [Assumption \u2014 below long-run nominal GDP ~4%, reflecting category maturity and innovation dependence].\nTerminal FCF = 1.094 \u00d7 1.035 = 1.132. TV = 1.132 / (0.097 \u2212 0.035) = $18.26B [Arithmetic].\nPV of explicit FCFs @9.7%: 0.686 + 0.676 + 0.682 + 0.694 + 0.688 = $3.426B [Arithmetic].\nPV of TV = 18.26 / 1.097^5 = $11.456B [Arithmetic].\nEnterprise value = $14.88B [Arithmetic].\nNet debt = $0.124B (my composition above).\nEquity value = $14.76B \u2192 per share = 14.76 / 0.1409 = $104.8 \u2248 $105. [Estimate]\n\nSensitivity of IV per share (9.7% WACC; base $105):\n\n| Terminal g / Terminal EBIT margin | 15.5% | 16.5% | 17.5% |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 2.5% | $91 | $105 | $119 |\n| 3.0% | $95 | $110 | $125 |\n| 3.5% | $99 | $115 | $130 |\n| 4.0% | $104 | $120 | $137 |\n\nExtending high growth (FY27-30 +10%, terminal margin 17%) \u2192 IV \u2248 $112-120 [Estimate]. Therefore, my Base-Case intrinsic value central range is $105-135, with a BASE point estimate of $120 and a conservative floor of $105.\n\nStep 3-3. Reverse DCF / Market-Implied Expectations:\n\nCurrent EV = $25.47B equity + $0.12B net debt = $25.59B. Under WACC 9.7%, g 3.5%, and five-year FCFs of $0.75-1.08B, the market's implied FCF2030 must be \u2248 $2.10B [Arithmetic]. That requires either (a) ~$12-13B revenue at a 17-18% EBIT margin (\u224812% CAGR over FY27-30), or (b) ~$11B revenue at a ~20% EBIT margin sustained. Both are feasible in a bull case, neither is the base case; both require flawless execution and no governance discount. Verdict: CURRENT PRICE TRANSLATES THE BULL CASE INTO THE BASE CASE.\n\nStep 3-4. Multiples Cross-Check:\n\n\u25cf Forward P/E: $6.50 EPS (guidance) \u2192 27.8x [Arithmetic]. High-quality consumer-discretionary compounders with mid-teens growth historically trade 20-30x; with FY27 growth decelerating to ~11-12%, fair multiple is 20-24x \u2192 fair price $143-156 [Estimate].\n\u25cf Trailing P/E 37.7x [Aggregator]; PEG 2.87 trailing [Aggregator] \u2014 >2.0 is expensive for a hardware grower.\n\u25cf EV/EBITDA: current EV $25.59B / FY26 adj EBITDA $1.365B = 18.8x [Arithmetic]. Peers (small appliances, quality consumer) 9-13x; growth premium to 13x \u2192 EV $17.7B \u2192 equity $17.6B \u2192 $125 [Estimate].\n\u25cf Average of methods: DCF $105-135; P/E $143-156; EV/EBITDA $125. Reconciled Base IV: $135. My conservative base: $120-135. MOUNTED MoS at $180.76 is NEGATIVE on every method.\n\nTornado (top 3 variables \u2014 these become Thesis KPIs):\n1. Terminal EBIT margin (\u00b11pp = \u2213$10-12/share).\n2. WACC (\u00b10.5pp = \u2213$9/share).\n3. FY27-28 revenue growth (\u00b12pp/yr = \u2213$8/share).\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5 \u2014 SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\n\u25cf Competitive response: If SN keeps winning in cooking/beauty, incumbents (Dyson, iRobot, Whirlpool, Chinese entrants via JD/Tmall) will respond with price and distribution moves. The cleaning decel to +4.1% may be the first evidence of pushback in the core. Effect: -2 (mildly negative).\n\u25cf Reflexivity: POSITIVE \u2014 strong equity gives low-cost SBC for talent, strong balance sheet shields supply-chain disruptions (they secured $247.1M tariff refund; smaller rivals did not). NEGATIVE \u2014 the Grizzly report and 41% insider/controller structure create a permanent governance overhang; any further allegation hits the multiple harder than the fundamentals.\n\u25cf Customer evolution: Early-adopter velocity (TikTok virality) is strong; mainstream penetration is the current phase \u2014 evidence: social commerce scaling to 14 countries; risk is that the late-adopter phase has structurally higher CAC and lower price elasticity. No recurring LTV/CAC data available [Unconfirmed] \u2014 treat any \"ecosystem\" claim as unproven.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 4 \u2014 SCENARIOS (BAYESIAN)\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\nPriors (Section 1.5): sustained rapid growth probability ~15-20%.\nPosterior update: 13 quarters of execution, raised guidance, $247.1M tariff refund, accelerating international \u2192 updates prior upward. Q2'26 growth +22.2% is itself information. Final probabilities:\n\n\u25cf BEAR (25%): Growth fades to mid-single-digit by FY28; terminal EBIT margin 14.5% (tariff annualization + competition); multiple compresses to 18x; governance allegations resurface. 12-mo price: $90-100. IV: $80.\n\u25cf BASE (50%): FY27 +11%, then fade to 6%; terminal EBIT 16.5%; multiple settles at 22x forward at a normal point in the cycle. 12-mo price: $145-160. IV: $120-135.\n\u25cf BULL (25%): International + TikTok + AI sustain 12%+ growth to FY30; EBIT margin 18%; valuation holds 28-30x forward. 12-mo price: $210-240 (consensus mean $209.56). IV: $190.\n\nExpected 12-month price = 0.25\u00d795 + 0.50\u00d7152 + 0.25\u00d7225 = $156 [Arithmetic].\n50% CI: $120-190 | 80% CI: $85-240.\nExpected return vs $180.76: \u221213.7% [Arithmetic]. MoS vs Base IV $135: (135-180.76)/135 = \u221233.9% [Arithmetic]. VERDICT: NEGATIVE margin of safety. The base case of the stock is a loss over 12 months.\n\nBayesian note: the bull scenario probability has already been partly \"bought\" by the market \u2014 the price is the aggregate belief. For NEW money at $180.76, the posterior probabilit